export anchor DeveloperPlatformStyle:
    number: 187
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Developer platform
    idea: A light developer console in indigo, where projects read like a list of build checks, figures sit in monospace and the overdue alert looks like a failed check annotation.
    base: light
    palette:
        indigo: #4338ca, the primary button, the current tab rule and icon, links and style sheet labels
        indigo2: #4f46e5, progress segments, heat level three and the focus ring
        indigoDeep: #312e81, the primary button border and heat level four
        indigoSoft: #c7cbfb, heat level two
        indigoTint: #eef0ff, heat level one, the avatar and the focused row
        background: #ffffff, the page, boxes and fields
        canvas: #f7f8fa, the header, box header strips and code chips
        ink: #1f2328, text
        muted: #5a6270, meta, monospace timestamps and labels
        line: #dadfe6, box borders, with #eaedf1 for row lines and empty segments
        onTrack: #17803d, On track with a circle and check
        atRisk: #94630a, At risk with a diamond and bang
        behind: #c62a2f, Behind with an octagon and cross, and the overdue annotation on #fdeced
    type:
        Two stacks. Sans is system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. Mono is ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Segoe UI Mono,
        Roboto Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The greeting is 22px sans at 650, box
        titles 14px sans at 650, body 14px sans, figures 16px mono at 600,
        and meta, dates, task counts and timestamps 12px mono.
    layout:
        A pale grey header holds a breadcrumb at left, an indigo code
        bracket mark, Brightwork in bold, a slash and home in mono, and at
        right a search field with a slash key hint, an indigo New project
        button, a square bell with an indigo dot and a square MO avatar.
        Under it the six nav items run as tabs with small icons, Home
        carrying a 2px indigo underline. The main area has the greeting
        Welcome back, Mara with Signed in as Mara Okafor and the date in
        mono, then a grid of a wide column and a 340px side column. The
        wide column has a Projects box whose grey header strip reads 6
        active, 4 on track, 1 at risk, 1 behind, then a pink annotation row
        with an octagon reading 4 tasks are overdue and a mono overdue 4.
        Each project is one checks row with a status badge, the name over
        team and mono task count, a ten segment progress bar, a mono
        percent, and the coloured status word with a mono due date. Under
        it an Activity box lists entries like a commit log with square
        initial tiles, item names in grey code chips and mono times below.
        The side column has a This week box of key and value rows split by
        dashed lines with mono figures, the overdue figure red, and a Tasks
        completed box drawn as a two row heat grid of fourteen cells, one
        row per week, Sunday to Saturday, each cell holding its number,
        with week totals 59 and 73 at the right, a green plus 14 note, an
        outlined today cell and a Fewer to More legend. Below 1060px the
        side boxes sit side by side under the main column. Below 720px tabs
        wrap without icons, the button shows only its plus, side boxes
        stack, and each check row wraps to name, bar and percent, then
        status and due date.
    spacing: A 4px base on an 8px rhythm. 24px gutters, 16px box padding, 10px row padding.
    density: Medium high. One line per project like a checks list.
    corners: 6px on boxes, buttons, fields and the avatar. 3px on heat cells and 4px on code chips.
    borders: 1px line on every box with a grey header strip, lighter lines between rows, dashed lines between key and value rows.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        16px line icons at 1.5 stroke on tabs and tools. Status uses solid
        16px badges with a white mark, a circle with a check, a diamond
        with a bang and an octagon with a cross, beside the coloured word.
    focus: A 2px indigo outline offset 2px. A focused field gets an indigo border and a 3px indigo tint ring, and a focused row takes the tint fill.
    tone: Terse and technical, such as 6 active, 4 on track, 1 at risk, 1 behind and overdue 4 in mono.
